From 19155599deae00dd16ab86356af82e2acf440505 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: genkigenki <3080081+genkigenki@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 21:11:12 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 045/240] BLE attempt 75: keep CLOCK SOURCE in bits 1-2 of the
 settings byte bt.

The clip keys use the settings bytes at offsets 38 and 39 (ck_x1, ck_x2).
a74 kept CLOCK SOURCE at offset 38, so a merge with clip-keys-a65 had a conflict in x0x.h.
Bits 1-2 of bt now hold CLOCK SOURCE, and bit 3 (PROJ_BT_CLK_IN) shows this layout.
Bit 0 of bt stays BLUETOOTH. The code reads bit 0 only with a mask.
settings_t stays 40 bytes, and offsets 38 and 39 are padding again, as on the merge base.
project_clk_check reads a project without bit 3 (a74 or older).
If offset 38 is 0-2 and offset 39 is 0, the value moves to bt and offset 38 becomes 0.
Thus a stale a74 value does not become ARP SWING 1 or 2 after the merge.
Else the load gives AUTO and does not change offsets 38 and 39.
A value of 3 in bits 1-2 loads AUTO.
project_clk_check runs before project_ck_check, so the clip keys check sees the clear offset 38.
The menu row, the values, the default AUTO and the clock code do not change.
clocksrc.x0x tests the new layout. BEHAVIOR.md: MID-13, SET-08.
