 MID-11. A USB bus reset or a deconfiguration clears the stored APC clip state. [CODE usb.c:554-559] [CODE usb.c:1113-1117] [CODE app/main_fm1.c:339-359]
-MID-13. GLO > MIDI > CLOCK SOURCE is the first row of MIDI, above CLOCK OUT. The values are AUTO, INTERNAL and EXTERNAL. The default is AUTO. SAVE and autosave keep it, as CLOCK OUT (SET-02). It uses the settings byte at offset 38, which was padding before. An older project loads AUTO, and a load sets a value more than 2 to AUTO. [USER] [CODE app/ui.c open_global] [CODE app/x0x.h settings_t.clk_src] [CODE app/project.c project_load] (New 2026-10-16, a74. The owner approved the design with all recommendations.)
+MID-13. GLO > MIDI > CLOCK SOURCE is the first row of MIDI, above CLOCK OUT. The values are AUTO, INTERNAL and EXTERNAL. The default is AUTO. SAVE and autosave keep it, as CLOCK OUT (SET-02). It uses bits 1-2 of the settings byte bt (offset 27). Bit 3 of bt shows that bits 1-2 hold the value. Bit 0 stays BLUETOOTH (BLE-05). A load sets a value of 3 to AUTO. A project without bit 3 comes from a74 or older. a74 kept the value 0-2 in the settings byte at offset 38, and offset 39 was 0. If offset 38 is 0-2 and offset 39 is 0, the load takes offset 38 as the value and sets offset 38 to 0. Else the load gives AUTO, and offsets 38 and 39 stay. The clip keys use offset 38 for ck_x1 (ARP SWING and HUMAN) and offset 39 for ck_x2. Thus a stale a74 value 1 or 2 does not become ARP SWING 1 or 2. A project of X0X 0.10 or a73 loads AUTO. [USER] [CODE app/ui.c open_global] [CODE app/x0x.h PROJ_BT_CLK_IN] [CODE app/project.c project_clk_check] (New 2026-10-16, a74. The owner approved the design with all recommendations. Changed 2026-10-16, a75: before, the value was at offset 38 only. Test: tests/scenarios/clkmove.x0x.)
 - AUTO: X0X follows a clock when one comes in, and it uses its internal clock when no clock comes in. This is the behaviour before a74 (MID-06, MID-12, LIM-11).
 - INTERNAL: X0X ignores MIDI Clock, Start, Continue and Stop from USB and Bluetooth. PLAY starts and stops X0X. The steps and the swing use the TEMPO value. When CLOCK OUT is ON, X0X always sends its clock, Start, Continue and Stop, also when a clock comes in. If X0X followed a clock at the change, each part's next step comes when the clock would give it.
 - EXTERNAL: X0X plays only on the incoming clock. It never sends clock, Start, Continue or Stop. MIDI Start, Continue and Stop act as in AUTO. PLAY with no clock arms X0X: the first tick plays step 1. PLAY again cancels.
