From 618182dbe7533241a2495c97525fc1d9b6b71b34 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: genkigenki <3080081+genkigenki@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 21:36:15 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 050/240] INLOG: record the inbound MIDI and the pad colours.

Add the read-only editor command ED_INLOG (38) on the SMK-37.
The firmware keeps the last 16 inbound messages in a ring.
Each entry has 2 words: the time in ms, and the source, status,
data 1 and data 2. Source 0 is USB, source 1 is BLE, source 2 is
a BLE link change (connected, notify on), source 3 is a BLE
message that the firmware did not use. The ring keeps only note
messages for the clip pads and the link changes.

Argument 0 gives the ring and the 40 clip velocities and channels.
Argument 1 gives the 16 pad colours in the pad colour store and
the 16 pad colours in the LED driver data. Thus you can see if the
pads show a colour that is not in the clip cells.

tools/ble_autotest.py --diag-only shows the data as text
(tools/inlog_fmt.py). It writes MISMATCH when a pad does not
agree with its cell.

Tests: tests/smk_inlog_test.c (ring wrap and encoding) and
tests/inlog_tool_test.py (text output).
Cost: 488 B of app code, 0 B of RAM, 132 B of pool.
