+| 38 INLOG (SMK-37, read only) | 0: entries; 1: pads | 0: count n, the time now (ms), then 2 × n words (oldest first: time ms; source << 24, status << 16, data 1 << 8, data 2; source 0 USB, 1 BLE, 2 link change (bit 24 connected, bit 25 notify on), 3 BLE not used), each 5 × 7 bits, then 40 clip velocities and 40 clip channels. 1: the value 1, the pad 'changed' flag, then 16 pad colours from the pad colour store and 16 pad colours from the LED driver data, each 4 × 7 bits (GRB). tools/inlog_fmt.py shows them as text. |
 | 34 BT_TEST (X0X SMK-37 with Bluetooth) | op: 0 query, 1 clear the Bluetooth start block (as BLUETOOTH OFF), 2 restart the unit 200 ms after the reply (chip reset, never the update loader) | op, BLUETOOTH setting (0/1), start blocked (0/1), Bluetooth state (firmware/src/app/plat.h PLAT_BLE_*) |
 | 37 CTL_READ (X0X SMK-37 with Bluetooth, read only) | offset (3 × 7 bits, from the Bluetooth block start, flash 0x8B000), count (pairs, 7 bits; at most 224 bytes) | offset, the bytes (pack7). Only the 64 KiB Bluetooth block: an offset outside it gets no reply, the count stops at the block end. tools/fm1_install.py compares the CRC32 with ctl.img |
 
