From 67231bc2f1653dd20a52c33042753fc3c62cb989 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: genkigenki <3080081+genkigenki@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 21:37:01 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 051/240] BLE: do not use notes and control changes while
 notify is off.

Owner test a74 (PAD CLEAR FAIL): after Loopy went away, the pads
went dark, and then the clip colours came back.

When the central sets the MIDI notify off (CCCD 0), the link
stays up. The host still accepts MIDI writes. The host keeps old
writes in its queue, because it empties the queue only when the
link starts or ends. Thus ble_service cleared the cells, and then
it put Loopy's APC40 feedback in the cells again.

Now ble_service does not use a note or a control change from BLE
while notify is off (ble_glue.h ble_in_unheard). It records each
of these messages in the inbound recorder as source 3.
Clock and other real-time messages stay as before.

Test: tests/smk_clip_ble_notify_test.c (the real BLE-MIDI host,
glue and cell model). Before this change cases A2, A3, B and C2
fail. After this change all cases pass.
tests/ble_test.c checks ble_in_unheard.
Cost: 32 B of app code.
