Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 21:38:21 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 052/240] CLIP: clear the pads again 300 ms after Loopy goes
 away.

Owner request (a76): when the BLE link ends or notify goes off,
clear the clip cells and each pad colour store. Then clear them
again 300 ms later, to remove a late write.

smk_apc_ble_link now uses smk_apc40_lost_step (smk_apc40.h).
It clears at the link loss, as before. It clears again 300 ms
later, but only if Loopy did not come back (link up and notify
on). Each clear also sets the pad colour store (lcd.c padled_rgb)
to dark and marks it as changed. Thus the next frame sends dark
pads to the LED driver.

Test: tests/smk_clip_dark_test.sh runs the real clip code of
main_fm1.c and the real pad LED code of lcd.c. It checks each pad
colour store and the LED driver data (padled_buf) for 10 s after
Loopy goes away. Before this change, cases 3 and 4 (a clip write
100 ms after the link end, 250 ms after notify off) fail. After
this change all cases pass. If Loopy comes back within 300 ms,
its new colours stay (case 5). A USB clip message after 300 ms
shows (case 6).
tests/smk_apc40_test.py checks the new calls.
Cost: 80 B of app code.
