From d829ed499ecaad4d108546daf1746aa7e1f7f469 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: genkigenki <3080081+genkigenki@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 21:52:35 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 057/240] SMK arrows: in a menu, < and > step the value of the
 selected row.

In a menu list (GLO or the list of a page), < and > step the value of the selected row down and up, as ALGORITHM.
The row does not move.
This is also true when GLO is open in clip mode, and only smk_arrows reads < and > then.
A held arrow repeats: the first repeat comes after 400 ms, then one step each 80 ms, on the 16 ms frame tick.
The value stops at its ends (no wrap).
Action rows and section headers do nothing.
With no menu, < and > move SELECT one detent for each press, as before, with no repeat.
In clip mode with no menu, and while HOME is held, < and > do nothing, as before.
The new file smk_arrows.h has the route (arw_route) and the hold repeat (arw_frame).
The new function ui_menu_arrow in ui.c calls turn_ref, the function that ALGORITHM uses.
The function list_sub_arrow in ui.c is the hook for submenu rows. This lane has no submenu rows.
The FM-1 build does not change: the new ui.c code is only in the SMK-37 and host builds.
The host simulator gets the commands "arrow" and "clipmode" and the expect keys listsel, overlay, page, rowval, arrowsteps and setsize.
New tests: tests/smk_arrows_test.c and tests/scenarios/arrows.x0x.
BEHAVIOR.md: GEN-29, the new GEN-56, MID-07 (a fourth exception) and CLP-27.
The owner approved this change at 21:20 (+10).
Size against 38af0a0 (Elite build): app code +224 B (1308 B to 1084 B free), static RAM 0 B, pool 0 B.
