smk_apc_ble_event (main_fm1.c), as before through smk_apc_usb_event.
While notify is off, a note-on or note-off for notes 0-39 (a clip
cell, the pad colours) does not change the cell
(smk_apc40.h smk_apc40_ble_colour_unheard). The recorder keeps it
as source 3. It gets the same answer as before, so it goes to the
sound engine when clip mode is off and no APC40 host is seen.
All other notes and control changes work as before.
ble_glue.h ble_in_unheard is removed.

Tests: tests/smk_clip_dark_test.sh case 7 (real main_fm1.c code)
checks that other notes and control changes get the same answer and
the same transport feedback as through smk_apc_usb_event, and that
a pad colour note changes no cell. tests/smk_apc40_test.py checks
that ble.c drops no message. Both failed before this change.
tests/smk_clip_ble_notify_test.c uses the new check and passes.
BEHAVIOR.md CLP-18 and BLE-15, web/EDITOR_PROTOCOL.md and
BLE_ATTEMPTS.md row 76 give the exact rule.
Cost: 32 B of app code (620 B free). Pool headroom 8196 B.
