Subject: [PATCH 062/240] SMK arrows: give the clip keys page the arrows in
 clip mode with no menu (CLP-27).

The comments in main_fm1.c and smk_arrows.h and the docs no longer say that < and > do nothing in clip mode with no menu.
In clip mode with no menu, smk_arrows does nothing, and the clip keys page takes < and > (CLP-76).
With a menu list open, ck_controls masks < and >, and only smk_arrows acts, so one press gives one step.
The new test tests/smk_arrows_owner_test.py checks this rule in the source, because the clip keys code needs the device build.
It also checks that smk_arrows and the clip keys page use the same hold repeat times, 400 ms and 80 ms.
BEHAVIOR.md GEN-29 now says "clip mode off". SMK37.md and the ledger row 77 tell the same rule.
The firmware code does not change.
