Subject: [PATCH 064/240] Clip keys pages: hold < or > to repeat the step.

A press of < or > steps the last field at once, as before.
A hold steps again after 400 ms, then one step each 80 ms.
The field stops at its first or last value, and an end press does not call ck_set, so the notes stay.
If < and > are both held, no step occurs.
While a menu is open or no page shows, < and > do nothing, also during a hold.
The new helper ck_rpt in smk_clip_keys.h has the timing logic, and test_rpt in smk_clip_keys_test.c tests it.
