 scratch.

The PERF TEST keeps three test patterns and one sound (2928 B).
These buffers now use the 4 KiB main-loop scratch in x0x.c.
The save (LZ hash table) and the update session also use this scratch.
These jobs do not use the same bytes at the same time.

- Make the test patterns in phase 0 of perf_test_tick, not in
  perf_test_start. Phase 0 starts after the last save that can run.
- Move the decoded host message of ota.c to offset 0xC00.
  The M-UPGRADE handshake can write it in any main-loop pass.
- Add static asserts for the layout.
- Add the scenario perfsave: a SAVE while playing, then the PERF TEST.
- Add the test perf-scratch: the host with the device scratch layout
  must give the same test sound as the host with its own buffers.

Elite: static RAM -2928 B (94644 to 91716 B). App code -32 B.
Pool: no change. No change to the sound, the display or the controls.
