From 3beeefce2cdb9649ff80534d71b4411e6499445d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: genkigenki <3080081+genkigenki@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 22:47:17 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 076/240] MID-15: follow the MIDI clock of one input only.

With CLOCK SOURCE AUTO or EXTERNAL, the first input that sends Clock, Start or Continue gets the clock.
X0X ignores Clock, Start, Continue and Stop from the other inputs.
The input keeps the clock until it sends nothing for 0.4 s.
After its Stop and 0.4 s with no Start, a Start or Continue of another input gets the clock.
The reason: USB and Bluetooth clock together gave two times the tempo.
0.4 s is more than 3 clocks at 20 BPM and less than the 0.5 s clock loss of MID-12.
Thus another input gets the clock before X0X goes to its internal clock or waits.
INTERNAL ignores all inputs, as before.
usb.c, ble.c and midi_uart.c write the input in bits 4-5 of byte 0 of the packet.
The saved settings do not change.
Add tests/host/clk_lock_test.c and tests/scenarios/clklock.x0x.
Elite size: app code +192 B, static RAM +12 B, pool 0 B.
