From 355f9205c5adada48d85fb87a857bd4f83469a20 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: genkigenki <3080081+genkigenki@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 22:50:47 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 078/240] BLE-16: release the Bluetooth notes when the
 Bluetooth link ends.

ble.c puts one link-end packet into the MIDI in queue when the link ends.
The packet goes after the MIDI in of that tick, so no note of the old link comes after it.
A disconnect, BLUETOOTH OFF and a controller failure give the packet.
engine.c keeps a bit for each 303 note and each break slice that came from Bluetooth.
At the link-end packet, engine.c releases these notes.
The notes from USB stay.
X0X sends no MIDI message out for it.
The clip keys release (CLP-70) does not change.
The reason: a note from Bluetooth stayed on when the link ended.
Add tests/scenarios/blenotes.x0x and the host commands blelinkend and midiheld.
Elite size: app code +420 B, static RAM 0 B, pool 0 B.
