 LIM-11. In AUTO (the default, MID-13), while X0X follows an external clock, it sends no Clock, Start or Stop (CLOCK OUT is muted), so no clock loop occurs. A MIDI Start that arrives when no clock came in the last 0.5 s starts X0X on its internal clock. CLOCK OUT is on by default (SET-08). In clip mode, X0X does not echo a MIDI Start, Continue or Stop (seq midi_req). Until the first incoming tick it can still send internal clock ticks (0xF8) to the USB host. With clip mode off, X0X sends Start (0xFA) and clock ticks back to the USB host until the first incoming tick, as before (agent-rules 2). [CODE app/engine.c:472-475 midi_in] [CODE seq/sequencer.c:378-379] [CODE seq/sequencer.c:392-393] [CODE seq/sequencer.c:470] [CODE seq/sequencer.c:446-455] [CODE seq/sequencer.c:511-512] If the clock then starts while X0X plays, the first tick is tick 0 of the step that plays. The next step comes 6 ticks later (16ths). (Changed 2026-10-16, a72: before, the first tick played the next step at once, so X0X played one step ahead of the clock.) [CODE seq/sequencer.c seq_advance] INTERNAL always sends CLOCK OUT when CLOCK OUT is ON. EXTERNAL never sends clock, Start or Stop (MID-13).
