+LIM-13. Bluetooth MIDI (BLE-01 to BLE-16) has only part of its hardware tests (Stage 3: docs/plans/2026-10-15-ble-stage3-test-plan.md). The Mac link passed 3 rounds of 600 s with no disconnect (a59). The return path to the Mac works (a60). The iPhone link works on a67 (94285b5, owner test 2026-10-16 19:18). BLE-16 is in code (2026-10-16), with a host test only. The RF calibration values are the AC79 SDK demo board values, not the unit's own. The clocks given to the image (system 360 MHz, HSB 180 MHz, LSB 60 MHz) were measured on an FM-1, not on an SMK-37. [CODE ../hal/fm1_ble.h]
 LIM-14. The controller's poll and its interrupts run on core 1 between and inside audio jobs. A long poll can delay an audio job past the 8 ms limit, and then X0X holds core 1 (one core, no Bluetooth). Long flash operations park core 1, and a long park can drop the BLE connection. Units that cannot run core 1 (fm1-x0x#10) have no Bluetooth. [CODE ../hal/fm1_cpu1.h]
 LIM-12. Only the SMK-37 build is maintained. The FM-1 build is not maintained. Its link step fails because the XIP region overflows by about 648 B. The user accepts this. It is not a defect. [USER]
 
