From c1efe6c56a58baeb3d7708370d0cca44674cec91 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: genkigenki <3080081+genkigenki@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 22:43:30 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 083/240] Tools: add tools/quickcheck.sh, a quick check before
 a push (60 s or less); run_tests.sh can run named tests.

- tests/run_tests.sh <name>... (or X0X_TESTS="<name> ...") runs only the named tests.
- tools/quickcheck.sh <commit or worktree folder> does the incremental Elite build (with its build checks)
  and then runs only the tests that the changed files affect, 8 at a time, with the time scale 20.
  A test is affected if its command or a test source names the changed file, or by a path rule
  (for example firmware/src/app/ gives host-build and the scenarios). If nothing matches, a fast host-only set runs.
- For an older tree without the name filter, the script uses a filtered copy of run_tests.sh.
- The quick check is a dev run: it never takes the gate lock. Only the gate takes it.
- Output: "QUICK PASS <hash> <seconds> s" or "QUICK FAIL <hash> <seconds> s <reason>". It is not the gate.
