From e448969b2ebcfa251c577726cb4e18de2dc01cfc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: genkigenki <3080081+genkigenki@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 22:43:34 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 084/240] Gate: refuse a commit that is not on integration
 unless --trial; add tools/install_gate.sh.

- tools/gate.sh stops with "FAIL <hash> not on integration (use --trial)" if the commit is not on the integration
  branch of the box repository. With --trial it runs, but the result is a TRIAL: the file <tree>.trial.md,
  an index row marked TRIAL and an output line that starts with TRIAL. A trial never counts as a release PASS,
  never uses a result again and never writes <tree>.md.
- tools/install_gate.sh installs tools/gate.sh as x0x37_gate.sh and tools/gate_flashmap.py into the gate folder.
  It starts only when the gate lock is free and no x0x37_gate.sh process runs, and it holds the lock during the install.
  Each file goes to a temp file in the same folder, gets mode 555 and replaces the old file with mv -f.
  The folder mode is restored. If the gate is busy, it waits (at most X0X_INSTALL_WAIT, default 1800 s) and then stops
  with "NOT INSTALLED" and the reason.
---
 tools/gate.sh         | 31 ++++++++++++++++++++--------
 tools/install_gate.sh | 48 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 70 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)
 create mode 100755 tools/install_gate.sh

diff --git a/tools/gate.sh b/tools/gate.sh
index 373f088..5cea130 100755
--- a/tools/gate.sh
+++ b/tools/gate.sh
@@ -1,7 +1,11 @@
 #!/bin/bash
 # SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-only
 # Pre-install gate for the SMK-37 Elite firmware (Linux x86-64 box only). It does not touch a device.
-#   tools/gate.sh <commit or ref> [--force]
+#   tools/gate.sh <commit or ref> [--force] [--trial]
+# The commit must be on the integration branch of the box repository (X0X_INTEGRATION). Else the gate stops with
+# "FAIL <hash> not on integration (use --trial)". With --trial the gate runs any commit, but the result is a TRIAL:
+# it goes to <tree>.trial.md and to an index row marked TRIAL, the output line starts with TRIAL, and it never counts
+# as a release PASS. A trial run does not use a result again and does not write <tree>.md.
 # The gate makes its own worktree of the commit, and then it does these steps:
 #   0. it checks that each reference folder is at its pinned commit (X0X_REF_PINS),
 #   1. the Elite build, the Pro build (build/x0x-smk37.fwsc, for the package tests), the FM-1 build and
@@ -23,7 +27,7 @@
 # It writes one result file per tree to $X0X_RESULTS/<tree>.md and adds a line to $X0X_RESULTS/index.md.
 # The tree is a SHA-1 of "git ls-tree -r" without the *.md files. If a result for that tree exists,
 # the gate uses it again and does not build (--force builds again).
-# Output: one line, "PASS <hash>" or "FAIL <hash> <reason>". Exit code 0 or 1. The full log is in the worktree folder.
