When the clock goes to another input, the beat ring of the tempo measure starts again.
The first ticks of the new input give no tick period.
The measure starts from the tempo that X0X has now.
The reason: the 0.4 s gap stayed in the measure for about 10 beats, so 120 BPM showed as about 109 BPM.
Now the tempo stays within 1 BPM after at most 2 beats.
A clock stop just after the change keeps 120 BPM.
tests/host/clk_lock_test.c checks both cases in AUTO and EXTERNAL.
The test clock now keeps its tick times between calls.
