From 078ab9f96c6fbfde2ffc6ab94cd6e9baacb72827 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: genkigenki <3080081+genkigenki@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 23:01:47 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 088/240] MID-15: free the clock at once when the link of its
 input ends.

usb.c midi_link_check puts one link-end packet into the MIDI in queue when a link ends.
Bluetooth gives it at a disconnect, BLUETOOTH OFF and a controller failure.
USB gives it at a bus reset and when the USB frames stop for 100 ms (unplug or host asleep).
engine.c calls seq_clk_drop for that input, so the next clock of another input gets the clock at once.
The Bluetooth link-end packet also releases the Bluetooth notes, as before (BLE-16).
The reason: before, the other input waited 0.4 s after the link end.
Add the host command usblinkend and the link-end cases to clk_lock_test.c and clklock.x0x.
Elite size: app code +96 B, static RAM 0 B, pool 0 B.
