Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 23:20:42 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 099/240] Add the copy of the gate results to the Mac (install
 guard)

The install guard on the Mac needs index.md, the result files and the
gate logs. The Mac cannot connect to the box.

- Add tools/sync_results_to_mac.sh. The copy goes in one direction,
  from the box to the Mac.
  --pack (box): makes mac-sync/<YYYYmmdd-HHMMSS>.tar and the symlink
  latest.tar. The tar file has index.md, the result files and, for each
  logs folder of a result file, only gate.log, crc.txt and result.md.
  It also has SHA256SUMS.
  --unpack <tar> (Mac): examines the paths and the checksums, then
  copies the files into X0X_RESULTS_DIR (default
  ~/Documents/x0x37/gate-results). The logs go to logs/<box path>.
  All files that it writes are read-only. It deletes no file.
  The agent copies the tar file to the Mac with CopyFromBox, as for
  the firmware files.
- tools/require_gate_pass.sh: if /workspace/x0x37-results is not
  there, the default results folder is ~/Documents/x0x37/gate-results.
  If the logs folder is not there, the guard also looks in
  <results folder>/logs/<logs path>.
- tests/host/test_install_gate_guard.sh: add a pack and unpack case.
  The guard must use only the copy. Now 14 cases.
