From 0f5e1f7c4de6d47e882b62df316b75d9a0b4a4bf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: genkigenki <3080081+genkigenki@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 23:15:28 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 111/240] Tools: make the pad calibration start table for the
 firmware.

tools/apc_pad_colors.py --pad-h writes APC40_PAD_DEFAULT as
uint8_t [128][3] in decimal to firmware/src/app/apc40_pad_default.h
(the build's register address check rejects the 0xRRGGBB words).
The firmware does not include it yet.
tools/apc_colour_model.py: PAD_GAIN_TRIM (R, G, B) is a new tunable
trim after the white gains. The values do not change (trim 1, 1, 1).
--pad-override FILE: the entries marked ok in a calibration export
("padcal V R G B ok") replace the rule. The other entries stay.
tests/apc_palette_test.py checks the override. tests/apc40_tables_test.c
checks the new table form.
Reason: the pad calibration mode starts from this table (option B,
Orchestrator decision 2026-10-16 23:10).
The build uses 0 B more app code, 0 B more static RAM and 0 B more pool.
