From cf22520e264cd5a2f6adc01d46ca026efda949c6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: genkigenki <3080081+genkigenki@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 23:15:59 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 112/240] Pad calibration: add the logic without hardware
 (smk_padcal.h).

app/smk_padcal.h has the state of the pad calibration and its rules:
- page and pad to entry (8 pages of 16, entries 0-127), page step with wrap,
- knob nudge (1 level a detent below 32, 1 + level / 32 above, stops at 0 and 255),
- a knob turn marks the entry ok, PLAY toggles ok,
- the export word (R | G << 8 | B << 16 | ok << 24).
The firmware does not include it yet.
tests/smk_padcal_test.c tests the mapping, the nudge ends, mark ok and the
export word. run_tests.sh runs it as smk-padcal.
apc40_pad_default.h includes stdint.h (the tool writes it).
The build uses 0 B more app code, 0 B more static RAM and 0 B more pool.
