From c71ea2a905833e989a60341e90f5240b5a3de439 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: genkigenki <3080081+genkigenki@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 23:21:18 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 113/240] Pad calibration: make the start values at run time
 from the LCD table.

The 384 B start table costs too much app code for the lane budget.
app/smk_padcal.h smk_padcal_default makes the start values of an entry
from its RGB565 LCD colour (the Akai colour): a 32-entry gamma table
(5-bit index, green uses its 5 high bits), Q8 white gains, the scale back
to the brightest decoded channel, and the floor (below it, the 5-bit codes
scaled to the floor, so the hue stays).
tools/apc_pad_colors.py --gamma-h writes the constants to
app/apc40_pad_gamma.h (PAD_GAMMA_LUT, PAD_GAIN_Q8, PAD_FLOOR_LEVEL).
tools/apc_colour_model.py pad_default does the same integer steps.
app/apc40_pad_default.h stays as the tool output (start values plus the
entries marked ok in an export). The firmware does not include it.
tests/smk_padcal_test.c: the firmware start values equal the tool output
for all 128 entries. tests/apc40_tables_test.c: the committed gamma header
equals the tool output.
The build uses 0 B more app code, 0 B more static RAM and 0 B more pool.
