From 4043ecf0cd79d669cf7217ac9adfc687921d4af7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: genkigenki <3080081+genkigenki@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 23:25:20 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 114/240] Pad calibration: add the mode GLOBAL > SYSTEM > PAD
 COLOURS.

The 16 pads show one page of 16 palette entries (8 pages, 128 entries)
at half level, as a lit clip pad. The LCD shows the Akai colour of each
entry in the same layout, a frame on the selected pad, a dot on each
entry marked ok, and the entry number of the selected pad.
A pad press selects the pad. K2 / K3 / K4 change R / G / B and mark ok.
SEQ PLAY marks ok or not ok. OCTAVE- / OCTAVE+ change the page.
PATCH or GLOBE ends the mode on the release.
The UI gets no buttons, keys or knobs meanwhile (plat_fm1.c, ui.c).
The row is not in the list in clip mode (the clip keys own the knobs).
The start values come at run time from APC40_LCD565 (app/smk_padcal.h).
The edits stay in RAM: no settings byte, no flash save.
BEHAVIOR.md CLP-79 is new. tests/smk_padcal_wiring_test.py checks the
wiring; tests/smk_apc40_test.py accepts the new key_event guard.
Reason: owner request 22:56 (pad calibration), option B.
The build uses 1200 B more app code, 416 B more static RAM, 0 B more pool.
