Subject: [PATCH 115/240] Pad calibration: export the entries over INLOG to the
 generator.

Editor command 38 INLOG, args 2-5, gives 32 entries each: R, G, B and
the ok bits, each 2 x 7 bits (main_fm1.c smk_inlog_reply). It works
also after the mode ends (the RAM stays until power off).
tools/inlog_fmt.py parse_padcal decodes a reply; padcal_lines writes the
export file ("padcal V R G B ok|-").
tools/ble_autotest.py --padcal-export FILE reads the four replies.
tools/apc_pad_colors.py --pad-h OUT --pad-override FILE puts the entries
marked ok over the start values.
tests/smk_padcal_export_test.py: the firmware words to reply bytes to the
export file to the generated header (round trip).
BEHAVIOR.md CLP-79 and web/EDITOR_PROTOCOL.md give the export.
The build uses 128 B more app code, 0 B more static RAM and 0 B more pool.
