From 0eab0fee76d1ae6ab9f9fd1b3135ed04030f168d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: genkigenki <3080081+genkigenki@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 23:37:20 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 118/240] Pad calibration: start with an orientation page.

The pad order on the unit is not proven.
PAD COLOURS now starts with an orientation page.
Only one pad is lit (white). The firmware takes this pad as top-left.
The LCD shows "pad 1 top-left?".
K2 moves the light to the next or previous pad (with wrap).
SEQ PLAY confirms the lit pad and goes to page 1.

The correction tl (0-15) stays in RAM.
Position i is on pad index i XOR tl (app/smk_padcal.h smk_padcal_phys).
tl 0: as assumed. tl 8: rows swapped. tl 7: rows mirrored. tl 15: both.
The pads and the pad presses use this rule.

The INLOG export (args 2-5) adds tl.
tools/inlog_fmt.py writes the line "padcal_orient TL".
tools/apc_pad_colors.py --pad-override warns if TL is not 0.

smk_padcal_test checks the identity map, the bijection and the four grid errors.
smk_padcal_export_test checks tl in the round trip and the warning.
BEHAVIOR.md CLP-79 gives the page and the rule.

The build uses 96 B more app code, 0 B more static RAM and 0 B more pool.
