Subject: [PATCH 127/240] Pad calibration: keep the edits when PAD COLOURS
 opens again.

Before, each open of PAD COLOURS set all 128 entries back to the start values.
The ok marks and the orientation correction also went back to their first values.
BEHAVIOR.md CLP-79 says that the edits stay in RAM until power off.

Now only the first open after power-on sets the start values (the RAM flag init in smk_padcal_t).
A second open keeps the entries, the ok marks and tl.
The orientation page then lights the pad of the saved tl, and the owner can confirm it again.

smk_padcal_test test_reopen fails on the old code and passes now.
The export test exports after a second open and finds the edits and tl.
The Elite build uses 0 B more app code, 0 B more static RAM and 0 B more pool.
---
 BEHAVIOR.md                   |  2 +-
