From 48892fe1270647102fd41348a6b38fdc25bb9fb8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: genkigenki <3080081+genkigenki@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 00:58:02 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 140/240] Clip pads: use the owner-calibrated pad table
 APC40_PAD_OWNER (CLP-13).

The owner made the export on 2026-10-17 with PAD COLOURS on build 89f680e. The file is
tools/padcal/pads-owner-20261017.txt (sha256 54ecc6f87ff0a0da). It has 128 entries, 89 ok and
padcal_orient 0. tools/apc_pad_colors.py --pad-name APC40_PAD_OWNER writes app/apc40_pad_owner.h
from the export. The 39 entries with no ok mark keep the 89f680e start values. The start-value
inputs did not change since 89f680e.

smk_pads sends the table level x brightness / 510 for a clip pad. The brightness is 255 or 0, so
a lit pad sends level / 2. These are the bytes that PAD COLOURS sent for the same entry. The dev
build and the release build use the same table. This commit removes APC40_RGB.

New test apc40_pad_owner_test.py. smk_apc40_violet_test.py now compares the violet entries with
the export, and the a76 hue range is information only. apc_pad_source_test.py stays out of
run_tests.sh as evidence. inlog_fmt.py and inlog_replay_fixture.py read the new table.
