Subject: [PATCH 147/240] LCD clip map: an idle square shows half of the full
 shade of its colour group (CLP-05).

Loopy sends a clip that does not play in the darkest shade of an Akai group (velocities 7, 11,
15 ... 59). On the LCD these squares were about 10 % of the full shade. The owner found the
colours hard to tell apart.

The LCD now shows half of the full shade (velocity v - 2). The tool halves each 8-bit Akai channel
(round half up) and makes RGB565 with the same rule as APC40_LCD565. tools/apc_pad_colors.py
--lcd-idle-h writes the 14 values to app/apc40_lcd_idle.h. app/smk_clip_colour.h smk_clip_lcd565
selects the value.

Velocities 0-6, the other shades and 60-127 do not change. Velocity 63 is not in
a shade group, so it does not change.

Loopy sends the same shade for an empty slot (LIM-03), so empty slots also get brighter.
SMK_CLIP_IDLE_LIFT 0 turns the change off. The pads and APC40_LCD565 do not change.
New test smk_clip_idle_test.py. It fails on f9bcc46 and passes now.
