Subject: [PATCH 148/240] Clip pads: an idle pad sends the full owner table
 level (CLP-13).

Loopy sends a clip that does not play in the darkest shade of an Akai group (velocities 7, 11,
15 ... 59). For these velocities the pad now sends APC40_PAD_OWNER x brightness / 255. That is
2 x the old level / 2. The owner asked for slightly brighter idle pads (01:17, level 01:19).

APC40_PAD_OWNER does not change. All other velocities send level x brightness / 510, byte-exact as
before. A table value of 0 stays 0, and no value goes above 10. app/smk_clip_colour.h
smk_clip_pad_level makes the byte. SMK_CLIP_IDLE_PAD_LIFT 0 turns the change off. Empty slots get
brighter too (LIM-03).

New test smk_clip_idle_pad_test.py. It fails before this commit and passes now.
apc40_pad_owner_test.py keeps the owner render check for the 114 other velocities.
