From b8255f2887e83f316d29d4466921f8e7030783cc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: genkigenki <3080081+genkigenki@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 01:47:20 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 149/240] Pad calibration: the selected LCD square shows
 brighter and shows its name (CLP-79).

The LCD square of the selected entry shows the colour with a gain of 2, 4 or 8. The gain is the largest that keeps each RGB565 field in its range. SEQ REC shows the real level. The other squares, the pads, the stored values and the export do not change. The LCD shows the name of the selected entry (hue family and shade from the Akai colour) and the gain.

tools/apc_pad_colors.py --names-h makes app/apc40_pad_names.h, and --names-csv makes docs/padcal-names.csv. The names are not Akai names and not Loopy Pro names. The code is in dev builds only. The release x0x.bin is identical to 4113ce0 (sha256 eeec5e83).

Owner request 2026-10-17 01:42, correction 01:43. Test: tests/padcal_view_test.py.
