From dbb86dbe88df0a49beb006678bd03a5bc7475b50 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: genkigenki <3080081+genkigenki@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 01:59:27 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 150/240] Test: a USB link end clears only the USB clip cells.

Owner report 2026-10-17 01:28 on f9bcc46: Loopy on the Mac uses USB.
When the owner pulls the USB cable, the pads keep the Loopy colours.
Owner fact 2026-10-17 01:46: Loopy on the Mac (USB) and Loopy on the
iPhone (Bluetooth) run at the same time.

The test tests/host/smk_clip_usb_clear_test.sh runs the real usb_poll
and ep1_rx of usb.c with a model of the SIE registers. It also runs
the real clip code of main_fm1.c and the real pad code of lcd.c.

Case U: Loopy sends 16 colours on USB. Then the cable goes out: no
SOF, the frame number stops, and the suspend interrupt comes. The
pads must go dark.

Case X: USB writes cells 0-3 and Bluetooth writes cells 8-11. A USB
end clears only cells 0-3. A Bluetooth CCCD 0 or link end clears only
cells 8-11.

Case L: when the two links write the same cell, the last writer owns
the cell.

Case C (Loopy quits on the Mac, owner 01:49): Loopy offs on channels
1-16 clear the cells (C1). A generic-mode SysEx (0x40) on USB clears
the USB cells (C2).

Case D (Loopy closes on the iPhone): a Bluetooth off while notify is
off clears the cell (D1).

On 4113ce0 cases U1, X1, X2, X3, L1, L2, C2 and D1 fail. usb.c sets
usb.suspended, but no code clears the cells. A Bluetooth end clears
all cells. Generic mode clears no cell. A Bluetooth off while notify
is off does not go to the cell.

The test is not in tests/run_tests.sh, because it fails before the
fix. Run it with: sh tests/host/smk_clip_usb_clear_test.sh
