From: genkigenki <3080081+genkigenki@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 01:59:27 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 151/240] Clip pads: a link end clears only the cells of that
 link (CLP-18).

Owner report 2026-10-17 01:28 and owner orders 01:46 and 01:49.
The owner uses Loopy on the Mac (USB) and Loopy on the iPhone
(Bluetooth) at the same time.

Each clip cell now has an owner link: the link that wrote the cell
last (main_fm1.c apc_ble_owned, one bit for each cell). When a link
ends, smk_apc_link_clear clears only the cells of that link. If a
cell stays lit, the latched layout does not change, so the pads of
the other link do not move.

USB: usb_poll gives the link state (configured and not suspended) to
smk_apc_usb_link. When the cable goes out or the host sleeps, the USB
cells clear. Before, only SET_CONFIGURATION 0 and a bus reset cleared
the cells, and they cleared all cells. apc_host_on and the notes do
not change at a cable-out or a sleep.

Bluetooth: a link end or CCCD 0 clears only the Bluetooth cells.
Before, it cleared all cells. Then the USB feedback of the Mac put the
colours on the pads again (case D).

Generic mode: the APC40 introduction with mode 0x40 on USB or
Bluetooth clears the cells of that link (case C).

While notify is off, an off from Bluetooth goes to the cell. Only a
colour note-on stops, as before.

Tests: tests/host/smk_clip_usb_clear_test.sh is now in
tests/run_tests.sh (smk-clip-usb-clear). On the base, cases U1, X1,
X2, X3, L1, L2, C2 and D1 fail. After this change all cases pass.

tests/smk_clip_dark_test.c now sends the Bluetooth feedback through
smk_apc_ble_event and the USB feedback through smk_apc_usb_event. Its
case 7 uses colour notes only. tests/smk_apc40_test.py checks the new
calls. BEHAVIOR.md CLP-18 and BLE-15 give the rule.

Elite app code free: dev 2520 B to 2312 B, rel 4088 B to 3928 B.
RAM .data+.bss: dev 92896 B to 92912 B, rel 92480 B (no change).
