From: genkigenki <3080081+genkigenki@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 02:57:09 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 165/240] Clip keys: a stage tap keeps the page open, and a tap
 again closes it (CLP-62).

A tap on SCALE, CHORD or ARP that turns the stage on opens its page and pins it (as FADER BANK pins it). A tap that turns a stage off closes the open page and removes the pin. A tap on another stage that turns it on moves the page to that stage. A hold works as before. FADER BANK closes the pinned page, and the stage stays on. Clip mode exit closes the page (as before).

CK_TAP_MS stays 300 ms. The knob paths do not change.

Owner request 2026-10-17 02:49, answers 02:51. Test: tests/smk_clip_keys_test.c test_page_latch.
