Subject: [PATCH 170/240] Tests: drum-pan and stereo wait for host-build
 (build/gen).

The tests drum-pan and stereo include build/gen/x0x_drum_tables.h.
host-build writes this file. In a fresh tree with parallel jobs,
drum-pan sometimes started before host-build. Then drum-pan failed.

Now a test in needs_gen starts only after host-build ends. It does
not hold a job slot while it waits. host-build is now before
drum-pan in the list. Thus a serial run also writes build/gen first.

The new host test gen-order runs drum-pan, stereo and host-build
in a fresh copy of the tree with 8 jobs and with 1 job. On c6bf44a
it fails with 8 jobs and with 1 job.
