From cea86b865249bf998ab683d23467c8de3d792818 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: genkigenki <3080081+genkigenki@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 02:56:48 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 175/240] Status: write only to the output folder of the run

Check 30 of rules v4. The status script takes an output folder.
Use "status.sh --out DIR" or X0X_STATUS_OUT=DIR. The default stays the live orchestrator folder for cron.
With another output folder, the temp files go to DIR/.status-tmp.

The test runner sets X0X_TEST_RUN. Then the script refuses the live folder with exit 4.

The new test status-isolation checks the refusal, the two output options and a scan of the status tests.
It also compares the live status.md and LIVE_BRANCHES before and after the status tests.
The bad fixture leaky_status_test.sh runs the script with no output folder. The scan must flag it.
