Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 02:59:51 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 179/240] Installer: refuse a package whose bootloader bytes
 differ from the unit

Check 4 of rules v4, Orchestrator decision 02:55. The bootloader is flash 0 to 0x4000.
The installer compares the sha256 of these package bytes with the sha256 of a reference read-back.
A different sha256 gives REFUSED and exit 11. The installer then opens no device.

The reference is --head-ref FILE, X0X_HEAD_REF or ~/.config/x0x/flash-head.bin.
With no reference, the installer writes a note and continues.
The installer has no flash read-back over USB-MIDI. The slot backup has only the sample slots.
The new option --head-check compares a package with a reference and opens no device.

The test install-head builds a small package. The fixture head_cases.txt changes one byte of the reference for each bad case.
