 script change

Check 5 of rules v4. The gate runs itself through the new wrapper gate_sigwrap.py. The wrapper keeps the PID of the gate.
On SIGTERM, SIGINT or SIGHUP the wrapper reads the PID, the folder and the command of the sender.
The KILLED line in gate.log and the KILLED output line then name the sender.

Check 13 of rules v4. The gate keeps the mtime of its script and of gate_flashmap.py.
A change during the run gives a SCRIPT CHANGED line in gate.log. The result does not change.

The test gate-trap stops a gate run on a temp repository. The fixture build.sh waits in the build step.
install_gate.sh now also installs gate_sigwrap.py.
