 (CLP-62, CLP-63).

The owner says that SCALE, CHORD and ARP are for the keybed, so Loopy can
record those notes. Case K10 turns the knobs with the page closed and open.
It also turns them after a stage tap and while you hold CHORD. Then it turns
them while you hold clip pads and after Loopy feedback. The knobs must set
the stage that a tap turned on last. The root knob and the chord knob must
change the notes of the keys. Knob 7 must send no old CC after the stage
goes off. K10 fails on 54f92b2 (5 fail).
